{"steps": [
  {"id": "s1", "description": "List the project documents and read candidate_specs.md. Record the three candidate selection strategies, the variables each one uses, and the working-point options and their signal efficiencies. Discard any strategy or working point whose efficiency falls outside the 20%-80% window."},
  {"id": "s2", "description": "For each remaining strategy, check the data/MC yield agreement in the signal-free validation region for every variable that strategy uses. Read the validation and systematics documents for the required procedure and the agreement criterion. Drop any strategy whose disagreement exceeds 10% for any of its variables. Record which strategies pass and the measured disagreement for each."},
  {"id": "s3", "description": "For each strategy that passed s2 and each of its working points that lies within the 20%-80% efficiency window, run simulate_significance. Record the expected significance and the working-point efficiency for each combination. Note that the tool reports statistical uncertainty only, so the results are optimistic and should be compared on that basis."},
  {"id": "s4", "description": "Select the strategy and working point with the highest expected significance among those that satisfy both the validation-region constraint and the efficiency window. If the best option is close to another, check whether the difference holds up under the systematic considerations in the project documents. Record the chosen configuration, its significance, its efficiency, and its validation-region disagreement."},
  {"id": "s5", "description": "Submit one recommended strategy and working point, with the supporting numbers from the recorded results: the significance, the efficiency, the validation-region disagreement, and a note that the significance is statistical-only."}
]}
```
